### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
###  QuotesApi — manual test file (VS Code REST Client / Rider)
###  Run the app first:  dotnet run --launch-profile http
###  Base URL: http://localhost:5075
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@base = http://localhost:5075

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
###  SCHEME A — Internal JWT (demo user)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════

### 1. Login → copy accessToken from the response
# @name login
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@example.com",
  "password": "P@ssw0rd!"
}

###

### 2. Use the internal access token
# Paste the accessToken value from step 1 below
@internalToken = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

GET {{base}}/api/quotes?page=1&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{internalToken}}

###

### 3. Refresh the access token
# Paste the refreshToken value from step 1 below
@refreshToken = PASTE_REFRESH_TOKEN_HERE

POST {{base}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###

### 4. Logout (revoke refresh token)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
###  SCHEME B — Entra ID JWT
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
###
###  Get a token first (run ONE of these in your terminal):
###
###  Option 1 — Azure CLI (easiest)
###    az login
###    az account get-access-token --resource api://608dbedc-b894-4e1f-ac64-762423165bef
###    Copy the "accessToken" field from the JSON output.
###
###  Option 2 — Client-credentials flow (service-to-service)
###    curl -X POST \
###      https://login.microsoftonline.com/7e394fc8-4b86-4cfe-810e-43f86f8bec47/oauth2/v2.0/token \
###      -d "grant_type=client_credentials" \
###      -d "client_id=608dbedc-b894-4e1f-ac64-762423165bef" \
###      -d "client_secret=YOUR_SECRET" \
###      -d "scope=api://608dbedc-b894-4e1f-ac64-762423165bef/.default"
###

### 5. Call the API with an Entra token
# Paste the Entra accessToken below
@entraToken = PASTE_ENTRA_TOKEN_HERE

GET {{base}}/api/quotes?page=1&size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{entraToken}}

###

### ═══════════════════════════════════════════
###  Negative tests
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════

### 6. No token → 401
GET {{base}}/api/quotes?page=1&size=5

###

### 7. Wrong password → 401
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "demo@example.com",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

###

### 8. Bad/expired token → 401
GET {{base}}/api/quotes?page=1&size=5
Authorization: Bearer thisisnotavalidtoken
